{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/844895-cofd-videogame-ideas","id":844895,"title":"CofD videogame ideas","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-03-09T20:55:05-08:00","id":844895,"title":"CofD videogame ideas","content":"So, from what we're hearing, it's looking like there's no chance of getting any ChroD games from Paradox, thus simultaneously disproving the existence of a benevolent god while proving the existence of at least three satans. <br /> <br /> So, anyway, what games set in the ChroD universe would you like to see? Pitches, concepts, random thoughts or bits, whatever. <br /> <br /> I'll start- a &quot;blue book&quot; survival-horror game based on the God-Machine Chronicle. You play a private investigator who somehow gets &quot;infected&quot; with a strange stigmata that draws ghosts and spirits to them and generally makes their life hell. A demon appears before them and offers to remove the brand, if they perform a series of increasingly dangerous and morally dubious tasks. The final one is to essentially destroy the personal life of an old friend of the protagonists, now an extremely wealthy CEO, so that the demon can convince him to sign a soul pact and take his life and fortune for itself. One possible ending involves betraying the demon and summoning an angel to kill it. The final scene shows the protagonist seemingly living a normal life, but reveals that contact with the angel essentially turned them into a God-Machine sleeper agent, who can be &quot;activated&quot; at any time and forced to do whatever task the machine needs done.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5358-geckopirateship","name":"Geckopirateship","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5358_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1383"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-09T21:04:01-08:00","id":844901,"title":"","content":"A relatively free-form Vampire game is an easy sell. Vampire: the Masquerade games, but Requiem.<br /> <br /> I proposed a beat-em-up game using Mummy a while back.<br /> <br /> A Changeling interactive story from Tell-Tale Games would be nice.<br /> <br /> I think Promethean is perfect for a very story driven solo game. Maybe Sandbox, even.<br /> <br /> I think one could get some mileage out of Werewolf as a Turn-based or Real-Time-with-Pause Tactical Game (with a bit of &quot;mission&quot; variety).<br /> <br /> Legacy of Kain: Soul Reaver -&gt; Geist: the Sin-Eaters. Maybe even a similar plot starter: you are seeking the one who betrayed and killed you.<br /> <br /> Hunter done up similar to X-Com, but with monsters instead of aliens (complete with the horrid attrition rate).<br /> <br /> Blue Books have so many options it is hard to mention.<br /> <hr /><br /> Basically, anything other than Mage, because getting Creative Thaumaturgy right in a pre-programmed environment would be <i>hard</i>.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":7212,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","user":"Vent0","date":". 03-10-2016, 12:06 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-09T22:00:00-08:00","id":844917,"title":"","content":"Chronicles of Darkness: Tokyo ( by Bethesda ) (seriously I think a &quot;Modern&quot; cityscape game by the people who bring us fallout and elderscrolls would be great)<br /> <br /> Werewolf the Forsaken a game of team tactics, lead your pack against the hordes of the shadow, by Bioware (ok the shifting animation would suck, but your interactions with your pack and the wolfblooded would be awesome), and your pack would actually work as a team, but for some damn reason you can only bring 1 or 2 of them with you...<br /> <br /> The God Machine by Frictional Games (Amesia a dark descent). Slowly descend into a mad world where a machine controls everything, but it didn't plan for you, or did it.<br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.pinterest.com/xenoterracide/chrod-inspirations/\" target=\"_blank\">Graphic Inspirational Photos for Chronicles of Darkness on Pinterest</a> <br /> <a href=\"https://chroniclesofdarkness.slack.com\" target=\"_blank\">Chronicles of Darkness Slack</a> (PM Me with Email for an Invite, then invite your friends)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4046-xenoterracide","name":"xenoterracide","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"563"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-09T22:00:37-08:00","id":844919,"title":"","content":"I would do horrible, evil things to have Paradox ask Obsidian to make another spiritual successor to Planescape: Torment, but using Mummy: The Curse as the setting. Promethean would be fantastic in that sort of story based cRPG too.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><a href=\"https://tinyurl.com/2p8ss75f\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Chris H</b></a>/<b>EndDaysEngine</b> | <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/EndDaysEngine\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Patreon</b></a></span>| <b>He/His </b>| <b>Currently Writing</b>: <i>[Redacted], [Redacted]</i><br /> <br /> <b>CofD booklists: </b><a href=\"https://goo.gl/DRdB7h\" target=\"_blank\">Beast</a> I <a href=\"https://goo.gl/x1FPpM\" target=\"_blank\">Changeling</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/ZSCx5U\" target=\"_blank\">Demon</a> | <a href=\"http://shorturl.at/syDK9\" target=\"_blank\">Deviant</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/Mh5M6m\" target=\"_blank\">Geist</a> l <a href=\"https://goo.gl/gSjfm5\" target=\"_blank\">Hunter</a> l <a href=\"https://goo.gl/qj5aX9\" target=\"_blank\">Mage</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/2HCpjg\" target=\"_blank\">Mummy</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/68yRHY\" target=\"_blank\">Promethean</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/a4mjqA\" target=\"_blank\">Vampire</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/hrULtN\" target=\"_blank\">Werewolf</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4433-second-chances","name":"Second Chances","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4433_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4202"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-09T22:02:26-08:00","id":844921,"title":"","content":"Promethean should be an MMO because you band together for a short amount of time for a goal and then disband just as quickly, no one really cares about you :evil:","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.pinterest.com/xenoterracide/chrod-inspirations/\" target=\"_blank\">Graphic Inspirational Photos for Chronicles of Darkness on Pinterest</a> <br /> <a href=\"https://chroniclesofdarkness.slack.com\" target=\"_blank\">Chronicles of Darkness Slack</a> (PM Me with Email for an Invite, then invite your friends)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4046-xenoterracide","name":"xenoterracide","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"563"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-09T22:12:13-08:00","id":844925,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Second Chances</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/844895-cofd-videogame-ideas?p=844919#post844919\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I would do horrible, evil things to have Paradox ask Obsidian to make another spiritual successor to Planescape: Torment, but using Mummy: The Curse as the setting. Promethean would be fantastic in that sort of story based cRPG too.</div> </div> </div> </div>As always, you beat me to the punch. I've said the exact same thing on my blog in the past.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-09T22:46:38-08:00","id":844931,"title":"","content":"I feel like there might be conceptual space for a Beast RTS.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-09T23:27:51-08:00","id":844944,"title":"","content":"For a long while, I wanted a full-on Werewolf game. You'd be able to switch freely between members of your pack and have different shot-calling tactics depending on who you were leading at a given moment. The sandbox areas would consist of several NPC packs with different allegiances and ideologies and you'd have the chance to recruit some of them instead of building your own pack. It'd be very Assassin's Creed, in terms of what you had to do to secure a territory (the way Syndicate played out is actually pretty close to what I had in mind). Three big groups in each neighborhood: the humans, the spirit courts, and the local Uratha pack: each with their own agendas, each playing off each other, and doing it mostly unknowingly, so you'd have to go-between them all. Doing missions for/about a particular group would change the influence that group had on the neighborhood, which would mess with the local ecology in weird ways. It'd be even more fun if you copycatted the Nemesis system from Shadow of Mordor and never really seemed to kill off the other Uratha; they'd just slink off, get stronger, and come back to challenge you again. It works for Werewolf better than almost anything else.<br /> <br /> In terms of down-to-earth gameplay, you'd want to play up shapeshifting as much as possible, which means downplaying combat. Instead, the game would be about stacking up dominos, doing a half-dozen mini-missions to set up possibilities and then letting those contingencies collapse as you wrapped up the hunt. Play up a lot of status effects rather than instant kills; when you murder a dude, they become a body and stop being fun. When you <i>mess</i> with a dude, they keep generating fun for the next ten minutes while you screw with everyone else. And then you can come back and mess with him again. A promise from a spirit here, an agreement with a human there, misdirecting a fellow Uratha for a crucial moment, and a conveniently empty and windowless room that your target walks into just after you do. I could see a nifty little scoring system for comboing a lot of things together into the perfect storm.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I call the Integrity-analogue the &quot;<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/822559-trying-to-understand-the-morality-system?p=825008#post825008\" target=\"_blank\">subjective stat</a>&quot;.<br /> An explanation how to <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/913221-using-social-manuevering\" target=\"_blank\">use Social Manuevering</a>.<br /> Guanxi Explanations: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/787518-the-mysterium-and-their-contribution-to-mage-society?p=787824#post787824\" target=\"_blank\">1</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/787518-the-mysterium-and-their-contribution-to-mage-society?p=788173#post788173\" target=\"_blank\">2</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/833863-mages-and-trading-favors?p=834531#post834531\" target=\"_blank\">3</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2758-errol216","name":"Errol216","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2758_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1112"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-09T23:39:32-08:00","id":844948,"title":"","content":"The three videogames I'd want are:<br /> <br /> 1. Geist: The Sin-Eater game similar to the first The Darkness game. Where you play a torn, who is betrayed at the start of the game and try to get revenge or at least justice. Give it a larger focus on side-missions though with getting info on your various targets by doing into the underworld or asking ghosts, helping people deal with ghosts that are fettered to their family, etc.<br /> <br /> 2. Hunter: The Vigil game similar to the first-person Grand Theft Auto V. My first thought when I played GTAV with first-person was &quot;I wish there were creepy lovecraftian monsters hiding in plain sight rarely in the world.&quot;<br /> <br /> 3. Mummy: The Cursed game similar to Darksiders/God of War. Where you use your immense powers to annihilate your foes throughout the ages.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/904596-geniuses-and-gramarie\" target=\"_blank\">Genius templates</a>: Super Science Mini-Template for Demon: the Descent<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1337874-oracle-the-endbringers-fan-splat\" target=\"_blank\">Oracle the Endbringers</a>: Time-Manipulator Fan-Splat","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8331-milo-v3","name":"milo v3","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8331_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1505"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-10T05:06:58-08:00","id":845023,"title":"","content":"Text-based game with crude, possibly just ASCII, GUI only for certain maps. Located in city and surroundings, with access to a couple neighboring towns and cities and instances within more far-flung exotic locales. Sandbox but with overarching plot and dynamic plots and events as well as some randomized occurrences. Character is fully player-made, overarching story would lean heavily on the character's choices.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-10T07:47:47-08:00","id":845075,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>xenoterracide</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/844895-cofd-videogame-ideas?p=844917#post844917\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Chronicles of Darkness: Tokyo ( by Bethesda ) (seriously I think a &quot;Modern&quot; cityscape game by the people who bring us fallout and elderscrolls would be great)</div> </div> </div> </div>Mortal, Mortal+, or what Splat?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>xenoterracide</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/844895-cofd-videogame-ideas?p=844917#post844917\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Werewolf the Forsaken a game of team tactics, lead your pack against the hordes of the shadow, by Bioware (ok the shifting animation would suck, but your interactions with your pack and the wolfblooded would be awesome), and your pack would actually work as a team, but for some damn reason you can only bring 1 or 2 of them with you...</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, there is always something else for the Pack to do. Just rotate Justifications that only allow you to take X number on &quot;trips&quot;.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>xenoterracide</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/844895-cofd-videogame-ideas?p=844917#post844917\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The God Machine by Frictional Games (Amesia a dark descent). Slowly descend into a mad world where a machine controls everything, but it didn't plan for you, or did it.</div> </div> </div> </div>Damned overflow calculation errors.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>xenoterracide</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/844895-cofd-videogame-ideas?p=844921#post844921\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Promethean should be an MMO because you band together for a short amount of time for a goal and then disband just as quickly, no one really cares about you :evil:</div> </div> </div> </div>Nah. There aren't really enough Created. Demon would be better. You never know if you can trust anyone.<br /> <br /> &quot;Why do you need 20 Cryptid asses?&quot;<br /> &quot;It's for an Occult Matrix. Not do you have them or not?&quot;<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/844895-cofd-videogame-ideas?p=844931#post844931\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I feel like there might be conceptual space for a Beast RTS.</div> </div> </div> </div>RTS? I can see the Lair as Base, but where would the units come from?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>milo v3</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/844895-cofd-videogame-ideas?p=844948#post844948\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The three videogames I'd want are:<br /> <br /> 1. Geist: The Sin-Eater game similar to the first The Darkness game. Where you play a torn, who is betrayed at the start of the game and try to get revenge or at least justice. Give it a larger focus on side-missions though with getting info on your various targets by doing into the underworld or asking ghosts, helping people deal with ghosts that are fettered to their family, etc.</div> </div> </div> </div>Totally.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>milo v3</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/844895-cofd-videogame-ideas?p=844948#post844948\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">2. Hunter: The Vigil game similar to the first-person Grand Theft Auto V. My first thought when I played GTAV with first-person was &quot;I wish there were creepy lovecraftian monsters hiding in plain sight rarely in the world.&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>Hunter seems kinda team-focused to do a FP. Promethean might work better. You could even liken the &quot;police attention&quot; to &quot;Disquiet Level&quot;.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>milo v3</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/844895-cofd-videogame-ideas?p=844948#post844948\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">3. Mummy: The Cursed game similar to Darksiders/God of War. Where you use your immense powers to annihilate your foes throughout the ages.</div> </div> </div> </div><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/809010-mummy-as-a-video-game\">Yes</a>. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":7212,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","user":"Vent0","date":". 03-10-2016, 10:58 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-10T08:08:49-08:00","id":845085,"title":"","content":"Old fashioned RPG Changeling 2.0","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2241-omegaphallic","name":"Omegaphallic","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-10T10:48:32-08:00","id":845164,"title":"","content":"Eternal Darkness like mystery, puzzle, horror RPG surrounding the Mystery Play leading up to the protagonist Awakening. Decisions the player makes affect the Path their character ends up on, and in turn colors some of the stranger parts of the game with that Path's imagery.<br /> <br /> Must play 5 times to see all the content!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Onyx Path Moderator </span><br /> <b>Mod Voice is <u><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">RED</span></u>*</b><br /> <i>*All other colors should be read aloud in the voice of Don Knotts</i><b>.</b> <hr /><b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/18519-pendragon-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\">Hacks and House Rules Hub Thread</a></b><br /> <br /> <b>CofD Hacks By Splat: <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/13vBLaS5Ua1Ez-cVyK6uFa4ssvYeIIZpoA5GQTXytfcA/edit\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#B22222\">Vampire</span></a> | <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1sqltG7X-C_MdEe00PtVOZmki8V_K1M1FpQtLwTvb2jg/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#006400\">Werewolf</span></a> | <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1bpr1EjQ4RfZ5dz-tXmJJ93P2f_l7fUIUwpPLWs9Z-SI/edit#\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800080\">Mage</span></a> | <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1vKpSTktCUuUaqxXncG4txQPtvPclzXlFZEEX7tbrTSg/edit#\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Mummy</span></a> | <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1Spynbcs_VgCDHdooKWXobZNe6C9CMjONeRTlvXIq9fI/edit?usp=drive_web\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Demon</span></a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/148-pendragon","name":"PenDragon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar148_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1657"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-10T10:52:12-08:00","id":845166,"title":"","content":"I think that new trend of RPG games with pre-definied protagonist and cinematic narration would fit CofD better than oldschool rpgs, mostly because player characters in old school rpgs were usually a character-less blank states with no personality, which doesn't help with the &quot;personal horror&quot; angle at all. Occult Alpha Protocol would be golden. For the same reason, I'm not a fan of Scrolls of Darkness Bethesda game. Tell-Tale Style adventure games also would be great, because honestly, I think that a lot of CofD settings would work better with predefinied protag with predefinied powers so developers can focus on how to potray it and only it in a best way.<br /> X-Com Hunter sounds great, on the other hand. I wouldn't mind procedural generated games in style of Overfall or X-Com or similar.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9102-whw","name":"WHW","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9102_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2542"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-10T11:02:16-08:00","id":845175,"title":"","content":"Eh, I'd kind of disagree with that- the whole reason I, and I think a lot of other people, play TRPGs or prefer them over videogames is the flexibility in creating a character. <br /> <br /> Plus, in the videogame industry, having a set protagonist tends to default to John Stubblegundad: His Wife Is Dead And They Took His Son<br /> <br /> Sadly, nofather's awesome idea will probably only exist in the alternate universe where Tarn Adams got into horror instead of fantasy.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5358-geckopirateship","name":"Geckopirateship","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5358_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1383"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-10T11:35:54-08:00","id":845194,"title":"","content":"I think a Sandbox game from Bethesda could work... as long as they partner with Bioware or Obsidian for the actual plot and dialog.<br /> <br /> It'd be great if they went with a more dark, cell-shaded look (similar to The Wolf Among Us). Might help prevent the dreaded Uncanny Valley effect that also plagues their games. <hr /><br /> I really think Promethean would be a great splat for it, too. Wooden or terse responses can be attributed to the whole &quot;learning to be human&quot; thing, said PCs usually travel a great deal and are independent. The more free-form nature of plotting is great for a &quot;complete what Milestones you wish&quot; pacing.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":7212,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","user":"Vent0","date":". 03-10-2016, 02:46 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-10T12:15:13-08:00","id":845206,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>milo v3</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/844895-cofd-videogame-ideas?p=844948#post844948\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The three videogames I'd want are:<br /> 3. Mummy: The Cursed game similar to Darksiders/God of War. Where you use your immense powers to annihilate your foes throughout the ages.</div> </div> </div> </div>I find it very interesting how Mummy lends itself to this epic, blow everything up type of playstyle (which is not a slam BTW, Darksiders and Dante's Inferno are two of my favorite games), as well as a deeply intimate, personal story of loss and suffering like Torment. It really shows the strength of the gameline. <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><a href=\"https://tinyurl.com/2p8ss75f\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Chris H</b></a>/<b>EndDaysEngine</b> | <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/EndDaysEngine\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Patreon</b></a></span>| <b>He/His </b>| <b>Currently Writing</b>: <i>[Redacted], [Redacted]</i><br /> <br /> <b>CofD booklists: </b><a href=\"https://goo.gl/DRdB7h\" target=\"_blank\">Beast</a> I <a href=\"https://goo.gl/x1FPpM\" target=\"_blank\">Changeling</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/ZSCx5U\" target=\"_blank\">Demon</a> | <a href=\"http://shorturl.at/syDK9\" target=\"_blank\">Deviant</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/Mh5M6m\" target=\"_blank\">Geist</a> l <a href=\"https://goo.gl/gSjfm5\" target=\"_blank\">Hunter</a> l <a href=\"https://goo.gl/qj5aX9\" target=\"_blank\">Mage</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/2HCpjg\" target=\"_blank\">Mummy</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/68yRHY\" target=\"_blank\">Promethean</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/a4mjqA\" target=\"_blank\">Vampire</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/hrULtN\" target=\"_blank\">Werewolf</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4433-second-chances","name":"Second Chances","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4433_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4202"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-10T13:09:02-08:00","id":845226,"title":"","content":"An Archmaster &quot;god mode&quot; game in which you develop cultures, species and nations and send them to war against NPC opponents or rival players. Includes Raid Boss Events like god kings getting out of control or an abyssal breach which would require groups of players working together.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Shachar%20Gold\" target=\"_blank\">Check my STV content</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/28219-my-weekly-wod-project-program\" target=\"_blank\">Or My Homebrew</a><br /> <br /> &quot;And all our knowledge is, Ourselves to know&quot;- An Essay on Man<br /> <br /> I now blog in <a href=\"https://chroniclesoflostlight.wordpress.com/\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/503-lostlight","name":"LostLight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar503_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4531"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-10T17:40:54-08:00","id":845373,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vent0</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/844895-cofd-videogame-ideas?p=845075#post845075\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Mortal, Mortal+, or what Splat?<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>All of the above, Bethesda games always have a ton of factions and a ton of characters on top of that... I think they could handle it. Maybe you start mortal and can get changed which works for everything but Demon really...","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.pinterest.com/xenoterracide/chrod-inspirations/\" target=\"_blank\">Graphic Inspirational Photos for Chronicles of Darkness on Pinterest</a> <br /> <a href=\"https://chroniclesofdarkness.slack.com\" target=\"_blank\">Chronicles of Darkness Slack</a> (PM Me with Email for an Invite, then invite your friends)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4046-xenoterracide","name":"xenoterracide","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"563"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-10T17:42:03-08:00","id":845374,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vent0</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/844895-cofd-videogame-ideas?p=845194#post845194\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think a Sandbox game from Bethesda could work... as long as they partner with Bioware or Obsidian for the actual plot and dialog.<br /> <br /> It'd be great if they went with a more dark, cell-shaded look (similar to The Wolf Among Us). Might help prevent the dreaded Uncanny Valley effect that also plagues their games. <hr /><br /> I really think Promethean would be a great splat for it, too. Wooden or terse responses can be attributed to the whole &quot;learning to be human&quot; thing, said PCs usually travel a great deal and are independent. The more free-form nature of plotting is great for a &quot;complete what Milestones you wish&quot; pacing.</div> </div> </div> </div>I always wanted a Bioware Bethesda team up... though not sure the current bioware is the bioware I want. Though I thought, get Id, or Valve to be on graphics, they're better at the pretty.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.pinterest.com/xenoterracide/chrod-inspirations/\" target=\"_blank\">Graphic Inspirational Photos for Chronicles of Darkness on Pinterest</a> <br /> <a href=\"https://chroniclesofdarkness.slack.com\" target=\"_blank\">Chronicles of Darkness Slack</a> (PM Me with Email for an Invite, then invite your friends)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4046-xenoterracide","name":"xenoterracide","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"563"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-10T21:48:01-08:00","id":845456,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>xenoterracide</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/844895-cofd-videogame-ideas?p=845373#post845373\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> All of the above, Bethesda games always have a ton of factions and a ton of characters on top of that... I think they could handle it. Maybe you start mortal and can get changed which works for everything but Demon really...</div> </div> </div> </div> \u200bWhy not Demon? You thought you were human, truly believed it, but that was just an Angel's cover until the day you were called upon to complete your purpose only to refuse and fall. <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6084-2pttakrill","name":"2ptTakrill","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"942"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-10T21:58:26-08:00","id":845463,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>2ptTakrill</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/844895-cofd-videogame-ideas?p=845456#post845456\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> \u200bWhy not Demon? You thought you were human, truly believed it, but that was just an Angel's cover until the day you were called upon to complete your purpose only to refuse and fall.</div> </div> </div> </div>You, Madame, Sir, of Soul, are an evil genius. Totally brilliant. <br /> <br /> I'm also wondering if a 2D Metriodvania couldn't work for pretty much every gameline. Each would take some tweeking to the formula for sure, but an old school side scroller like that could be fun. That and programs like <a href=\"http://www.stencyl.com/\" target=\"_blank\">Stencyl</a> are a thing.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><a href=\"https://tinyurl.com/2p8ss75f\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Chris H</b></a>/<b>EndDaysEngine</b> | <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/EndDaysEngine\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Patreon</b></a></span>| <b>He/His </b>| <b>Currently Writing</b>: <i>[Redacted], [Redacted]</i><br /> <br /> <b>CofD booklists: </b><a href=\"https://goo.gl/DRdB7h\" target=\"_blank\">Beast</a> I <a href=\"https://goo.gl/x1FPpM\" target=\"_blank\">Changeling</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/ZSCx5U\" target=\"_blank\">Demon</a> | <a href=\"http://shorturl.at/syDK9\" target=\"_blank\">Deviant</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/Mh5M6m\" target=\"_blank\">Geist</a> l <a href=\"https://goo.gl/gSjfm5\" target=\"_blank\">Hunter</a> l <a href=\"https://goo.gl/qj5aX9\" target=\"_blank\">Mage</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/2HCpjg\" target=\"_blank\">Mummy</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/68yRHY\" target=\"_blank\">Promethean</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/a4mjqA\" target=\"_blank\">Vampire</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/hrULtN\" target=\"_blank\">Werewolf</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4433-second-chances","name":"Second Chances","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4433_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4202"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-10T22:13:29-08:00","id":845466,"title":"","content":"How about a Mage game where you play as a Guardian Of The Veil. Your job in the city is to find which supernaturals are getting too careless and encourage them to be more subtle. You'd be encouraged to use diplomacy and other non-violent methods. There could be levels where you infiltrate Oneiroi and enemy bases in the Invisible Realms a la Psychonauts, levels where you interview people and investigate crime scenes like in L.A. Noir, and levels where you must chase a supernatural with a time limit while keeping vulgar spellcasting to a minimum similarly to Assassin's Creed and Prototype. The stealth mechanics could borrow from the Batman: Arkham _______ trilogy, Metal Gear and Splinter Cell. Instead of a police suspicion meter (Quiescence and off-screen Mind spells would handle that), you'd have a Paradox accumulation meter for spellcasting too carelessly, which can lead all the way up to a Manifestation if you're unlucky. You'd use a lot of mind-reading and security hacking too, like in Destroy All Humans and Watchdogs, respectively. And the final boss would have to be someone genuinely unexpected, but not completely out of the blue or trite. There might not even be a fight. I know I was pretty amazed by the encounter with Andrew Ryan in Bioshock 1.<br /> <br /> Would anyone here play that?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Bye.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4443-gibberingeloquence","name":"GibberingEloquence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4443_5.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2470"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-10T22:21:34-08:00","id":845470,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/844895-cofd-videogame-ideas?p=844931#post844931\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I feel like there might be conceptual space for a Beast RTS.</div> </div> </div> </div> What kind of RTS are you imagining? I feel like the RTS games I know lack the personal approach the Begotten have with their Kin. Hundreds of units on the screen at the same time and such.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Bye.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4443-gibberingeloquence","name":"GibberingEloquence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4443_5.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2470"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-10T22:29:50-08:00","id":845473,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>GottaGoFeast</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/844895-cofd-videogame-ideas?p=845470#post845470\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> What kind of RTS are you imagining? I feel like the RTS games I know lack the personal approach the Begotten have with their Kin. Hundreds of units on the screen at the same time and such.</div> </div> </div> </div>Inadequacies of language and lack of encyclopedic knowledge of genres. TBS games are generally too mission-oriented to have the kind of tag-tracking involved and I found it easier to suggest a low-unit-count first-person RTS than to try and articulate a genre that I'm moderately certain doesn't technically exist.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-10T23:08:29-08:00","id":845488,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/844895-cofd-videogame-ideas?p=845473#post845473\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Inadequacies of language and lack of encyclopedic knowledge of genres. TBS games are generally too mission-oriented to have the kind of tag-tracking involved and I found it easier to suggest a low-unit-count first-person RTS than to try and articulate a genre that I'm moderately certain doesn't technically exist.</div> </div> </div> </div> So, maybe like an open-ended Team Fortress 2, where each playable unit has advantages and disadvantages. The tone might be somewhat similar: alternating between goofy and sadistic. Instead of borderline Slashers, you would control monster heroes like Jackie Estacado in The Darkness 1 &amp; 2. The gameplay might be focused on expanding your territory, Brood and shared Lair while climbing towards the status of Apex and/or Incarnate. Not sure how to translate that into concrete mechanics, though. Maybe something focused on gang warfare like in Saints Row?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Bye.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4443-gibberingeloquence","name":"GibberingEloquence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4443_5.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2470"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-11T04:17:08-08:00","id":845553,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>xenoterracide</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/844895-cofd-videogame-ideas?p=845374#post845374\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I always wanted a Bioware Bethesda team up... though not sure the current bioware is the bioware I want. Though I thought, get Id, or Valve to be on graphics, they're better at the pretty.</div> </div> </div> </div>Go play Witcher 3. It's the hybrid you desire, and it's pretty much better than anything both Bethesda and Bioware created in last...5? 6? 8? years. And actually, you can pretend it's a Hunter game set in fantasy world. Don't worry about it being a &quot;3rd&quot; game, it's self contained and you don't need to play or know previous entries. This and Alpha Protocol are pretty much my go-to &quot;how I imagine CofD games as RPG&quot;.<br /> <br /> As for Beast strategy game - look around for old RTS &quot;Sacrifice&quot;. It isn't really what you are talking about, but I think you could get some inspiration from there.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9102-whw","name":"WHW","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9102_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2542"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-11T05:13:14-08:00","id":845564,"title":"","content":"Blue Book + Beast= Amnesia the Dark Descent style game.<br /> <br /> Vampire + Werewolf= Stealth Based horror Game about evading though a werewolves Territory on the night of a Major ceremony.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Light and Dark are two Sides of a Coin... Humanity is What Happens when it Lands on it's Edge.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3981-rickmanuk","name":"RickmanUK","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3981_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"533"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-11T06:01:06-08:00","id":845582,"title":"","content":"I think Beast would be great as a more &quot;political&quot; game - you build alliances/kinships with the conflicting factions of supernatural, as you strive to become the Apex. Add a consequence/Chaos Meter, so the tone of your interaction and feedings influence future outcomes.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-11T17:49:00-08:00","id":845894,"title":"","content":"Metal Gear Falling: Techgnostic Espionage Action","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/526-schizopop","name":"schizoPOP","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"108"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-11T18:48:32-08:00","id":845913,"title":"","content":"A video game based on the already existing <a href=\"http://www.amazon.com/Vampire-Prince-Modern-Gothic-Requiem/dp/1565042743\" target=\"_blank\">Prince of the City</a> would be nice. Same with <a href=\"http://www.amazon.com/gp/product/1588467473/ref=pd_lpo_sbs_dp_ss_1?pf_rd_p=1944687522&amp;pf_rd_s=lpo-top-stripe-1&amp;pf_rd_t=201&amp;pf_rd_i=1565042743&amp;pf_rd_m=ATVPDKIKX0DER&amp;pf_rd_r=04FV7TB01X1NTS49RSFN\" target=\"_blank\">Deadly Prey</a>.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/604-shock","name":"Shock","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar604_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Po