 <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>SaulottheGentle</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/844895-cofd-videogame-ideas?p=846550#post846550\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Then it's Chronicles of Darkness related? There was a name change.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> out, it was stated that we're not getting CofD games.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B5_EJSgV1u4SOFFJc3M5VmFDWVk?resourcekey=0-GEErNnDbGqlKYgoiuGausw&amp;usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">My Bloodline conversions</a><br /> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1IbeKfqhWuG8jPN9vpGmDo0VY9n9-4ejxvRzfJRoir4k/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">My House rules</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/294-griautis","name":"Griautis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar294_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2293"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-16T18:07:38-07:00","id":848517,"title":"","content":"I was going to start a thread about a hypothetical CoD fighting game before I found this thread. I don't know if it would be 2D or 3D, but I'm a big fan of Skullgirls, Darkstalkers and Mortal Kombat, so that's what comes to my mind. I'd like one character for each major template. The second to last boss could be a newly awakened Mummy with lots of Biblical attacks that are hard to dodge and do a ton of damage. A lower Sekhem and higher Memory version of that Mummy would be an unlockable character. The final boss could be a Rank 6 Angel that you fight in an extradimensional or outer space Infrastructure. Stages would include more gothic-looking versions of those you find in other fighting games (e.g. a church, haunted house and a subway station), a few wilderness areas, and the four Invisible Realms.<br /> <br /> I don't have much more than that in mind, though. Does anyone have something they'd like to see in such a game?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Bye.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4443-gibberingeloquence","name":"GibberingEloquence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4443_5.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2470"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-16T18:54:29-07:00","id":848536,"title":"","content":"Persona 5 Arena is effectively a G:tSE fighting game.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/904596-geniuses-and-gramarie\" target=\"_blank\">Genius templates</a>: Super Science Mini-Template for Demon: the Descent<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1337874-oracle-the-endbringers-fan-splat\" target=\"_blank\">Oracle the Endbringers</a>: Time-Manipulator Fan-Splat","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8331-milo-v3","name":"milo v3","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8331_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1505"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-16T19:21:17-07:00","id":848555,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>milo v3</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/844895-cofd-videogame-ideas?p=848536#post848536\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Persona 5 Arena is effectively a G:tSE fighting game.</div> </div> </div> </div>There's my favorite Guilty Gear character, too, Zappa. Though I suppose he was more of a ghost host.<br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"><img src=\"http://www.fightersgeneration.com/nx9/char/x2-reload/zappa-x2-reload-artwork.jpg\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/></div></div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Geckopirateship</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/844895-cofd-videogame-ideas?p=845175#post845175\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Sadly, nofather's awesome idea will probably only exist in the alternate universe where Tarn Adams got into horror instead of fantasy.</div> </div> </div> </div>He did the inspiration for a single player variant, with a lot of MUD experience as the foundation.<br /> <br /> Lots of nice ideas in this thread.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":886,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","user":"nofather","date":". 10-26-2018, 01:37 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-27T17:10:06-07:00","id":854260,"title":"","content":"How about a 3D collect-a-thon platformer, like Crash Bandicoot, Spyro The Dragon, Psychonauts and Banjo &amp; Kazooie?<br /> <br /> I'm thinking the protagonist would be a Hero, and the levels would be Lairs you have to maneuver through while avoiding traps and dispatching enemies carefully. <br /> <br /> The bosses would be Beasts. To vary things and shed some light into Hero's delusion of grandeur, you'd have levels with a different type of gameplay, and a supernatural other than a Beast as the boss. <br /> <br /> The more of these side bosses you defeat, the clearer it would become that the Hero is doing all of this for selfish and petty reasons. There would be hints spread through the game that the Hero will come to a grisly and ignoble end. <br /> <br /> For example: the part of the main menu where you can browse the Hero's collectibles (e.g. heads of slain Beasts, stolen items of emotional significance to other monsters, newspaper clipings &quot;congratulating&quot; you for &quot;saving the day&quot;), you would see implications that the Hero can't hold down a job and has abandoned a well-adjusted family because of the all-important Quest. <br /> <br /> There could be sidequests where you can try to get back to your friends and family, but these would be presented as boring (i.e. no collectibles or bosses, just a few branching dialogue options) on purpose, to convey how addicted to fighting monsters the Hero has become. <br /> <br /> When you get to the very end of the last level, the build-up and foreshadowing get a shocking pay-off: you stop playing as the Hero and take control of an Incarnate. You are invulnerable and terrifying to behold, and the ensuing &quot;fight&quot; can be ended with a few button presses. The more you delay that, the more frustrated the Hero gets, until they realize how screwed they are and try to run away in terror. While running, the Hero tries to steal a motorcycle and dies in a mere traffic accident. <br /> <br /> The main menu part with the Hero's trophy room now shows the stolen items either confiscated by authorities or returned to where they belong.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Bye.","edited":{"userid":4443,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4443-gibberingeloquence","user":"GibberingEloquence","date":". 03-27-2016, 08:16 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4443-gibberingeloquence","name":"GibberingEloquence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4443_5.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2470"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-27T18:18:07-07:00","id":854288,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>atamajakki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/844895-cofd-videogame-ideas?p=846422#post846422\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Give me Crusader Kings/Total War where you play as either a Vampire elder or a Mummy. Can your mortal servants gain enough sway to impose your will on the world without exposing you to enemies and Hunters? Bonus points if you can customize your Cult somewhat and have to deal with heresies/schisms over the ages as generations of cultists mistranslate and misinterpret your wishes.<br /> <br /> It would be especially fun if after a certain number of turns you had to succumb to torpor/Duat, and then come to much later to see just how wrong things went.</div> </div> </div> </div> Have you ever heard of Dwarf Fortress? The goal is to manage your mostly independent dwarves so you can build the most epic and ludicrously convoluted fortress possible before things inevitably get out of hand and you get a game over. It is extremely minimalist in graphics, but detailed in gameplay (there are some packs you can download to make graphics easier to parse, I think). <br /> <br /> There is a Let's Play called <b><a href=\"http://tvtropes.org/pmwiki/pmwiki.php/LetsPlay/Boatmurdered\" target=\"_blank\">Boatmurdered</a></b> that can be seen as the total derailing of a project that gets made worse by each Mummy that picks it up.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Bye.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4443-gibberingeloquence","name":"GibberingEloquence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4443_5.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2470"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-27T18:41:46-07:00","id":854298,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>GibberingEloquence</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/844895-cofd-videogame-ideas?p=854288#post854288\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> Have you ever heard of Dwarf Fortress? The goal is to manage your mostly independent dwarves so you can build the most epic and ludicrously convoluted fortress possible before things inevitably get out of hand and you get a game over. It is extremely minimalist in graphics, but detailed in gameplay (there are some packs you can download to make graphics easier to parse, I think). <br /> <br /> There is a Let's Play called <b><a href=\"https://&amp;quot;http://tvtropes.org/pmwiki/pmwiki.php/LetsPlay/Boatmurdered&amp;quot;\" target=\"_blank\">Boatmurdered</a></b> that can be seen as the total derailing of a project that gets made worse by each Mummy that picks it up.</div> </div> </div> </div>I would hope the Arisen have learned about delicious lava well enough to avoid it in future Descents.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-27T18:46:13-07:00","id":854302,"title":"","content":"I'm not sure how in depth it is but there is <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/288270-princes-of-darkness-a-ck2-mod\">a mod for Crusader Kings II</a> to let you play as a vampire or werewolf inspired by World and Chronicles of Darkness.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-27T18:54:04-07:00","id":854305,"title":"","content":"I still say that a Werewolf RPG/GTA hybrid sort of thing would be great. Especially if you had a &quot;hunt planning&quot; feature similar to the heist planning feature from GTA V or Payday 2 (preferably a mix of the two, where you choose the general approach and which pack mates to take (Like in GTA V) and then get to go into the fiddly details like in Payday 2's heist planning mode) for the really important hunts. The regular hunts would have something like the planning screen for the smaller hunts in Payday 2.<br /> <br /> And of course, there would be a drop-in multiplayer option during the hunts where your friends could play the other werewolf packmates. Human packmates would have very specific jobs to do on hunts (Getaway driver/pilot, hacker, medic, surveillance expert that sort of thing) but would give an out of hunt benefit. Not sure where to fit in wolf blooded packmates. They are just powerful enough where average team AI won't cut it, but I'm not sure if players would go for them.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Despite the user name I am actually bigender.<br /> <br /> My Savannah Setting for CofD can be found <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/959455-the-young-man-in-the-cafe-s-savannah-georgia-setting-writeup\" target=\"_blank\">here</a><br /> <br /> My heroes as monster tamers rules for BtP can be found <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/975230-heroes-as-monster-tamers-rules-ideas\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":3932,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3932-the-young-man-in-the-cafe","user":"The young man in the cafe","date":". 03-27-2016, 10:08 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3932-the-young-man-in-the-cafe","name":"The young man in the cafe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3932_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1097"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-27T20:47:38-07:00","id":854346,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The young man in the cafe</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/844895-cofd-videogame-ideas?p=854305#post854305\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I still say that a Werewolf RPG/GTA hybrid sort of thing would be great. Especially if you had a &quot;hunt planning&quot; feature similar to the heist planning feature from GTA V or Payday 2 (preferably a mix of the two, where you choose the general approach and which pack mates to take (Like in GTA V) and then get to go into the fiddly details like in Payday 2's heist planning mode) for the really important hunts. The regular hunts would have something like the planning screen for the smaller hunts in Payday 2.<br /> <br /> And of course, there would be a drop-in multiplayer option during the hunts where your friends could play the other werewolf packmates. Human packmates would have very specific jobs to do on hunts (Getaway driver/pilot, hacker, medic, surveillance expert that sort of thing) but would give an out of hunt benefit. Not sure where to fit in wolf blooded packmates. They are just powerful enough where average team AI won't cut it, but I'm not sure if players would go for them.</div> </div> </div> </div> I'd play that. I assume the Shadow would be incorporated into a dual-world mechanic, but downplayed in comparison to all the preparation and risks already involved in the material realm.<br /> <br /> How do you think the Idigam should be used in a game like this? I think they should be an unpredictable/unscripted threat that can mess up your plans and/or the enemy's plans big time, sorta like Nemesis from Resident Evil. They'd need really dynamic AI and varied tactics to be properly mercurial. The behavior of the xenomorph in Alien: Isolation would be a good example.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Bye.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4443-gibberingeloquence","name":"GibberingEloquence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4443_5.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2470"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-28T06:19:41-07:00","id":854445,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>GibberingEloquence</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/844895-cofd-videogame-ideas?p=854346#post854346\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> I'd play that. I assume the Shadow would be incorporated into a dual-world mechanic, but downplayed in comparison to all the preparation and risks already involved in the material realm.<br /> <br /> How do you think the Idigam should be used in a game like this? I think they should be an unpredictable/unscripted threat that can mess up your plans and/or the enemy's plans big time, sorta like Nemesis from Resident Evil. They'd need really dynamic AI and varied tactics to be properly mercurial. The behavior of the xenomorph in Alien: Isolation would be a good example.</div> </div> </div> </div> Idigam definitely need to be a big chaos factor when it comes to the pack's plans. But they shouldn't be overused either. I think an idigam or it's minions should have a random chance of showing up on the major hunts, but actually killing the idigam is a major hunt in of itself. The idigam, in a way, are part of why I want the fiddly details like in payday 2. Having a plan B should be important on the hunt, even if you wind up not using it. Unlike in GTA V, where the complications are scripted, it should be possible to have the plan go off without a hitch if you're skilled and lucky, but you will want a plan B anyway in case something like an idigam happens.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Despite the user name I am actually bigender.<br /> <br /> My Savannah Setting for CofD can be found <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/959455-the-young-man-in-the-cafe-s-savannah-georgia-setting-writeup\" target=\"_blank\">here</a><br /> <br /> My heroes as monster tamers rules for BtP can be found <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/975230-heroes-as-monster-tamers-rules-ideas\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3932-the-young-man-in-the-cafe","name":"The young man in the cafe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3932_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1097"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-29T22:18:44-07:00","id":855497,"title":"","content":"A dungeon keeper like game where you play as a high preist for a Mummy's cult. After the Mummy leaves their enemies come and attack the tomb and it is up to you to protect the tomb. Then the mummy comes back and you can ask them for a favor, like ritualistically murdering a cultist and binding their ghost to surve as a guardian.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":7525,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7525-quinn-h","user":"Quinn H.","date":". 03-30-2016, 02:59 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7525-quinn-h","name":"Quinn H.","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"29"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-06T11:05:00-07:00","id":860435,"title":"","content":"I would like a game in the style of Shadowrun: returns, made by the same team. With any game line, I just want to play that. Or a tell-tale style game for geist.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11165-tangledvirus","name":"TangledVirus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11165_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-07T08:49:32-07:00","id":861076,"title":"","content":"I'd love a serie of RPG computer games based in ancient Irem. Similar to what Dragon Age is doing, expanding and developing their world with new games.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>LAND OF THE DAMNED: SPAIN (Spanish): </b><a href=\"https://goo.gl/3MHWYm\" target=\"_blank\">Land of the Damned: Spain</a>, <a href=\"https://goo.gl/52b0TX\" target=\"_blank\">Kingdoms of Blood: Spain</a>; Cities of the Damned: <a href=\"https://goo.gl/XFMSSe\" target=\"_blank\">Barcelona</a>, <a href=\"https://goo.gl/AXxdgq\" target=\"_blank\">Valencia</a>, <a href=\"https://goo.gl/zkI5a1\" target=\"_blank\">Carthian Constitution</a> (1812), <a href=\"https://goo.gl/5H8M4s\" target=\"_blank\">Three Arrows Pact</a>: <br /> <br /> <b>OTHERS (Spanish): </b><a href=\"https://goo.gl/36HngB\" target=\"_blank\">Demon: The Redemption</a>, <a href=\"https://goo.gl/6B9V8l\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Forgotten</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/247-uxas","name":"Uxas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar247_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"394"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-09T14:45:54-07:00","id":862770,"title":"","content":"An obsidian RPG set in the Neolithic setting","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7525-quinn-h","name":"Quinn H.","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"29"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-29T20:32:30-07:00","id":923665,"title":"","content":"I'm trying to think of an example of gameplay that would fit Promethean. The game has some similarities to Dark Souls, and the survivalist aspect could be like the one in Fallout, but focused on your Disquiet and Wasteland instead of the radiation. As mentioned before in this thread, Planescape: Torment is similar to both Mummy and Promethean in how it handles the theme of humanity. <br /> <br /> But how Disquiet be handled? Just through plot, or would there be a meter that increases and decreases depending on how you interact with NPCs? <br /> <br /> In any case, it should be light on combat and heavy on exploration and puzzle solving (which seems to be the goal of Athanors in 2ED). Perhaps like the Myst series?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Bye.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4443-gibberingeloquence","name":"GibberingEloquence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4443_5.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2470"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-29T21:46:06-07:00","id":923700,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>GibberingEloquence</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/844895-cofd-videogame-ideas?p=923665#post923665\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm trying to think of an example of gameplay that would fit Promethean. The game has some similarities to Dark Souls, and the survivalist aspect could be like the one in Fallout, but focused on your Disquiet and Wasteland instead of the radiation. As mentioned before in this thread, Planescape: Torment is similar to both Mummy and Promethean in how it handles the theme of humanity.<br /> <br /> But how Disquiet be handled? Just through plot, or would there be a meter that increases and decreases depending on how you interact with NPCs?<br /> <br /> In any case, it should be light on combat and heavy on exploration and puzzle solving (which seems to be the goal of Athanors in 2ED). Perhaps like the Myst series?</div> </div> </div> </div>Eh. It's not really dissimilar from Heat in various crime-ish games.<br /> <br /> I'd make it more complicated than a meter, though: I'd want some kind of alternate screen where you set a network of Important Things and the nature of how Disquiet and Wasteland manifest should come out of that. I'd have to think about it more (and preferably read the official 2e rules) to get a sense of what should be in that web.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I call the Integrity-analogue the &quot;<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/822559-trying-to-understand-the-morality-system?p=825008#post825008\" target=\"_blank\">subjective stat</a>&quot;.<br /> An explanation how to <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/913221-using-social-manuevering\" target=\"_blank\">use Social Manuevering</a>.<br /> Guanxi Explanations: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/787518-the-mysterium-and-their-contribution-to-mage-society?p=787824#post787824\" target=\"_blank\">1</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/787518-the-mysterium-and-their-contribution-to-mage-society?p=788173#post788173\" target=\"_blank\">2</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/833863-mages-and-trading-favors?p=834531#post834531\" target=\"_blank\">3</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2758-errol216","name":"Errol216","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2758_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1112"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-29T23:10:07-07:00","id":923720,"title":"","content":"Apologies if this has been mentioned elsewhere, but I feel that if there's a hunter game, it would have to be a bit of an XCOM clone with light base management and an emphasis on squad combat. Instead of skill tree progression, possibly a focus on upward movement in a compact/conspiracy?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/483-flyboy254","name":"Flyboy254","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar483_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"703"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-30T00:06:47-07:00","id":923741,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Flyboy254</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/844895-cofd-videogame-ideas?p=923720#post923720\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Apologies if this has been mentioned elsewhere, but I feel that if there's a hunter game, it would have to be a bit of an XCOM clone with light base management and an emphasis on squad combat. Instead of skill tree progression, possibly a focus on upward movement in a compact/conspiracy?</div> </div> </div> </div>Actually I think any Hunter-based videogame would be more similiar to Division than XCOM, but that's just my personal opinion.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11117-inquisitor","name":"Inquisitor","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11117_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"138"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-30T06:26:43-07:00","id":923809,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Inquisitor</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/844895-cofd-videogame-ideas?p=923741#post923741\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Actually I think any Hunter-based videogame would be more similiar to Division than XCOM, but that's just my personal opinion.</div> </div> </div> </div>But do your people drop like flies in Division?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-30T12:12:50-07:00","id":924008,"title":"","content":"I've always wanted a customizable slasher/Slasher game; like the upcoming Friday the 13th game, but more narrative and strategy elements, like Until Dawn or Hitman. Achievements for enforcing or avoiding tropes and conventions, bonus points and free-for-all ending for bringing down a tentpole convention like killing the Final Girl halfway through. Maybe play both sides, set off drama to split people up, find ways to match people's positions to their weaknesses, like placing the drinker sentry in a wet bar. Maybe just play cutscenes as influential outside characters, like the <a href=\"http://tvtropes.org/pmwiki/pmwiki.php/Main/HarbingerOfImpendingDoom\" target=\"_blank\">old man at the remote gas station</a>, or that Act 3 cop who <a href=\"http://tvtropes.org/pmwiki/pmwiki.php/Main/PoliceAreUseless\" target=\"_blank\">never seems to be able to help</a>, to make differences in the following scene.<br /> <br /> ...I feel like I've just red-flagged myself.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1289-hastur00","name":"Hastur00","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1289_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"366"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-30T12:21:42-07:00","id":924012,"title":"","content":"Sort of like Party Hard, but with a lot more work put into it? I could dig it. I always liked games where you can deal with issues in multiple ways. The Hitman franchise has been a favorite.<br /> <br /> I thought Dead by Daylight looked like a pretty good mortal versus Slasher video game.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"videocontainer with-aspect-ratio videocontainer-horizontal\" style=\"aspect-ratio: 16/9;\"> <a class=\"video-frame\" href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=JGhIXLO3ul8\" data-code=\"JGhIXLO3ul8\" data-provider=\"youtube\" data-height=\"0\" data-width=\"0\" itemprop=\"video\"> <div class=\"videothumbnail\" style=\"\"> <img src=\"https://img.youtube.com/vi/JGhIXLO3ul8/maxresdefault.jpg\" alt=\"\" /> <div class=\"videothumbnailoverlay\"></div> </div> </a> </div>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}